    <string name="examples_label">Stuck? Try one of these:</string>
    <string name="example_hotdog_label">🌭 Is a hot dog a sandwich?</string>
    <string name="example_hotdog_text">My friend Sam says a hot dog is a sandwich: it\'s a filling inside sliced bread, end of story. I say it\'s its own thing. Nobody orders a sandwich and expects a hot dog, and no menu lists it under sandwiches.</string>
    <string name="example_tomato_label">🍅 Is a tomato a fruit?</string>
    <string name="example_tomato_text">Alex insists a tomato is a vegetable because that\'s how everyone cooks and eats it. I say it\'s a fruit, because botanically it grows from the flower and carries the seeds.</string>
    <string name="example_white_lie_label">🤥 Are white lies OK?</string>
    <string name="example_white_lie_text">Jordan told a friend they loved her new haircut when they actually hated it, and says a white lie like that is just kindness. I think real friends should hear the truth, said gently.</string>
    <string name="example_knuckles_label">🦴 Does knuckle cracking cause arthritis?</string>
    <string name="example_knuckles_text">My mom says cracking my knuckles will give me arthritis. I crack them all the time and I say that\'s a myth with no evidence behind it.</string>
    <string name="example_pineapple_label">🍍 Pineapple on pizza?</string>
    <string name="example_pineapple_text">Riley says pineapple on pizza is a crime against Italian cooking. I say pizza is whatever tastes good, and tradition alone is not an argument.</string>
